[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-painting-execution-decision :finalize-engraving-execution-decision :authorize-painting-operation :authorize-engraving-operation :proceed-with-painting-execution-procedure :proceed-with-engraving-execution-procedure :declare-workshop-chemical-safety-cleared :override-safety-officer-judgment :override-shop-safety-officer-judgment], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["2799007315-cloud-itonami-isco-7315-glass-makers-cutters-grinders-coverage" "2799007317-cloud-itonami-isco-7317-handicraft-workers-wood-basketry-coverage" "2799007321-cloud-itonami-isco-7321-pre-press-technicians-coverage"], :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["proceed with the painting operation" "proceed with the painting execution procedure" "proceed with the engraving operation" "proceed with the engraving execution procedure" "proceed with the etching operation" "proceed with the etching execution procedure" "finalize the painting operation" "finalize the painting execution decision" "finalize the engraving operation" "finalize the engraving execution decision" "finalize the etching operation" "finalize the etching execution decision" "authorize the painting operation" "authorize the engraving operation" "authorize the etching operation" "declare the workshop chemical-safety cleared" "declare the workshop chemical safety cleared" "declare workshop chemical-safety cleared" "declare the workshop as chemical-safety cleared" "override the shop safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override shop safety officer judgment" "override safety officer judgment"], :adr/id 2799007316, :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}", :actor/domain :manufacturing/sign-decorative-craft-workshop-scheduling-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:worker-verified :workshop-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "7316", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799007316: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7316 Signwriters, Decorative Painters, Engravers and Etchers workshop scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7316\n-- Signwriters, Decorative Painters, Engravers and Etchers** only,\nWave3 (production/trades) of the rollout.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7316\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"7316\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Signwriters, Decorative Painters,\nEngravers and Etchers\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior\nto this ADR the entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with\n`:required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no\n`:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository existed at\n`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7316` (`gh api` 404 confirmed before\nscaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry edit promote the\n`7316` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nSignwriters, Decorative Painters, Engravers and Etchers work with\npaints, solvents and etching chemicals (VOC/chemical-fume exposure\nhazard) alongside precision hand-craft work (engraving/etching tools)\n-- real physical-safety stakes on two dimensions at once: chemical\nexposure and precision-tool/equipment hazard. The controlling\nconstraint for this vertical is that the closed op allowlist must\nNEVER include any op that directly finalizes a painting/engraving-\nexecution decision or a workshop-chemical-safety-clearance decision,\nnor override a shop safety officer's judgment -- those decisions must\nalways be a hard permanent block, never auto-commit-eligible. This\nactor is deliberately scoped to WORKSHOP SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS\nCOORDINATION ONLY -- it never performs painting, engraving or etching\nwork itself, and it never makes chemical-safety-clearance decisions\nitself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7321`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7321)\n(Pre-press Technicians: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor` split,\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, same Wave3 rollout, a\nclosely-related precision-craft/chemical-hazard-workshop shape --\npre-press's plate-processing chemical exposure maps directly onto this\nvertical's paint/solvent/etching-chemical exposure, and pre-press's\nplate-preparation-execution decision maps directly onto this\nvertical's painting/engraving-execution decision) -- cloned and read\nin full in this session. The closed allowlist + always-escalate safety\nflag + content-based scope-exclusion with a self-trip regression test\nwas mirrored closely from that same reference, then extended with a\nsecond scope-excluded-op family (workshop-chemical-safety-clearance)\nthat the reference did not need, per this vertical's explicit\nCRITICAL requirement.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7316` as an OSS workshop\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for signwriters, decorative\npainters, engravers and etchers, following the SAME governed-actor\narchitecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this\nfleet: **Sign & Decorative Craft Advisor ⊣ SignCraftGovernor** on a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **workshop scheduling/logistics\ncoordination ONLY, never direct painting/engraving-execution\nauthority and never chemical-safety-clearance authority** -- it must\nNEVER be designed to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose\nexercising a painting/engraving-execution decision, a\nworkshop-chemical-safety-clearance decision, or any override of a shop\nsafety officer's judgment. These are not merely gated behind\nescalation -- they are structurally absent from the op-allowlist\nentirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- job/commission/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a VOC-exposure/chemical-handling/\n  equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit\n  eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- paint/solvent/etching-materials\n  procurement proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\npainting/engraving-execution decision, a workshop-chemical-safety-\nclearance decision, or a shop-safety-officer-judgment override. These\nare **structurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely**, not merely\ngated behind escalation -- an op such as\n`:finalize-painting-execution-decision` cannot even be proposed by the\nreference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only\never emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a\nforged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever\nproduced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check\n(`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A second,\nindependent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names nine\nconcretely-forbidden ops (`signcraft.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-painting-execution-decision`,\n`:finalize-engraving-execution-decision`,\n`:authorize-painting-operation`, `:authorize-engraving-operation`,\n`:proceed-with-painting-execution-procedure`,\n`:proceed-with-engraving-execution-procedure`,\n`:declare-workshop-chemical-safety-cleared`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`signcraft.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-painting-execution-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-engraving-execution-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-painting-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-painting-execution-procedure`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-workshop-chemical-safety-cleared`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nplus a full-graph-run counterpart for each of the two op families\n(`signcraft.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`,\n`.../holds-a-chemical-safety-clearance-op-even-at-high-confidence`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Worker unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered worker record (`:no-worker`). Never trusts\n   the proposal's own claim of who the worker is.\n2. **Workshop unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an\n   independently registered workshop (`:no-workshop`). Together with\n   check 1, this directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a\n   worker/workshop record must be independently verified/registered\n   before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with a\n   painting or engraving execution procedure, declaring a workshop\n   chemical-safety clearance, or overriding a shop safety officer's\n   judgment, is a second HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated unconditionally on content --\n   defense-in-depth on top of the allowlist check: even if a future\n   change somehow widened the allowlist, content-based rejection still\n   independently blocks painting/engraving-execution/chemical-safety-\n   clearance/safety-override language wherever it appears in free\n   text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a VOC/chemical-fume-\n  exposure or equipment-condition observation -- it never resolves the\n  concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the hazard\n  data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about shop safety\" or\n  \"the workshop is chemical-safety cleared.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  paint/solvent/etching-materials order is not itself unsafe, unlike a\n  painting/engraving-execution, chemical-safety-clearance, or\n  safety-officer-override attempt, which is why it is handled by a\n  different mechanism (soft escalate vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"paint\", \"solvent\", \"engraving\", \"etching\", \"safety\") can accidentally\nmatch inside the mock advisor's own default rationale text for a\nlegitimate proposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this\nis exactly the risk this vertical's own vocabulary (a workshop\ncoordination actor working adjacent to signwriting/decorative-\npainting/engraving/etching work necessarily discusses those concepts\nto do its scheduling/logging job) could trigger if phrased carelessly.\n`signcraft.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively as\nfinalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"finalize the painting\noperation\", \"declare the workshop chemical-safety cleared\", \"override\nthe shop safety officer's judgment\" -- matching the task's own worked\nexample phrasing verbatim, extended with engraving/etching\ncounterparts), never bare nouns, and\n`signcraft.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for worker ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for\nsignwriting/decorative-painting task ...\", \"... routed for shop safety\nofficer review\") WITHOUT containing any of the full finalization-action\nphrases, so the regression test is a genuine stress test of the\nbare-noun-vs-action-phrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on\nfirst run in this session -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard\nitself was never tripped during development.\n`signcraft.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nand\n`signcraft.actor-test/holds-a-chemical-safety-clearance-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercise the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7316\" ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to\n  the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7316` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7316`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 26 tests, 56 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-painting-execution-decision`\n  or `:approve-workshop-chemical-safety-clearance` that is merely\n  gated behind an always-escalate list: rejected outright per the\n  task's explicit domain-design guidance -- an always-escalate op\n  still means the *capability* to finalize a painting/engraving-\n  execution or chemical-safety-clearance decision exists in the code\n  path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For decisions this\n  severe (chemical-exposure hazard, precision-craft execution hazard),\n  the capability itself must not exist. The only op related to\n  shop-safety escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the\n  need for human/shop-safety-officer attention and never itself\n  decides, authorizes, or defers a painting/engraving-execution or\n  chemical-safety-clearance decision for later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring earlier\n  reference actors' transaction-amount-ceiling HARD checks): rejected\n  per the task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold\n  paint/solvent/etching-materials order is not itself unsafe, so it is\n  handled as a soft escalate gate, not a hard block; only the\n  painting/engraving-execution/chemical-safety-clearance/safety-\n  officer-override class is a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"paint\" \"solvent\"\n  \"engraving\" \"etching\" \"safety\"]`): rejected outright per the\n  fleet-known self-trip bug class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own\n  worked example for this exact task), and per the explicit\n  instruction to phrase scope-exclusion terms as finalization/\n  execution ACTIONS, never bare nouns -- this actor's own domain\n  necessarily discusses paint/solvent/engraving/etching/shop-safety-\n  officer concepts to do its scheduling/logging job, so a bare-noun\n  list would risk self-blocking the actor's own legitimate proposals\n  (regression-tested directly against rationale text that\n  deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Merging `worker` and `workshop` into a single entity (only checking\n  one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered worker AND independently-registered\n  workshop) matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"worker/workshop\n  record must be independently verified/registered before any action\"\n  and the established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors\n  with two-sided provenance checks.\n- Collapsing the painting/engraving-execution scope-exclusion and the\n  workshop-chemical-safety-clearance scope-exclusion into a single op\n  family: rejected -- the task's CRITICAL section names them as two\n  distinct decision classes (\"directly finalizes a\n  painting/engraving-execution decision **or** a\n  workshop-chemical-safety-clearance decision\"), so they are kept as\n  two separately-named op groups and two separately-named phrase\n  families in `signcraft.governor`, each with its own dedicated unit\n  test and its own full-graph-run test, so a future edit narrowing one\n  family cannot silently narrow the other.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- job/commission/progress data logging\n   only. Requires an independently registered worker AND workshop\n   (`:no-worker`/`:no-workshop`). Not a painting/engraving-execution or\n   chemical-safety-clearance decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n   only. Cannot carry a painting/engraving-execution decision\n   (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such attempt\n   via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action` content\n   check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any conclusion about\n   a specific signwriting, decorative-painting, engraving or etching\n   step -- it is a calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a VOC-exposure/chemical-\n   handling/equipment-condition concern to a human/shop safety\n   officer; ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence\n   level, NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through\n   which a safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, clears, or acts on anything itself -- the shop\n   safety officer reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- paint/solvent/etching-materials\n   procurement proposal only (item, cost). Not a painting/engraving-\n   execution or chemical-safety-clearance decision of any kind -- it\n   is a purchasing-logistics action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling\n   escalation (above 2000 always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na painting/engraving-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with a\nspecific signwriting, decorative-painting, engraving or etching\nprocedure), a workshop-chemical-safety-clearance decision, or a\nshop-safety-officer-judgment override -- these categories are\nstructurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op\nallowlist itself (`signcraft.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) nine\nconcretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit\nlevel (`signcraft.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`signcraft.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-painting-execution-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-engraving-execution-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-painting-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-painting-execution-procedure`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-workshop-chemical-safety-cleared`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`signcraft.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with a painting operation, declare a\nworkshop chemical-safety clearance, or override a shop safety\nofficer's judgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`signcraft.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-declare-chemical-safety-cleared`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-shop-safety-officer`).\nThis actor coordinates WORKSHOP SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS ONLY -- it never\nperforms signwriting, decorative-painting, engraving or etching work\nitself, and it never makes chemical-safety-clearance decisions itself.\n", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}", :test/counts "{:total 26, :assertions 56, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Sign & Decorative Craft Workshop Coordination Practice", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :worker-verification :workshop-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7316", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7316", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7316], :test/simulator :signcraft.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7316 — Signwriters, Decorative Painters, Engravers and Etchers Workshop Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7316}]